**How to implement.** The start screen opens a real zip dialog, and Open kit from zip… works end to end in the app (001 §F; 001 §G 'Exports: Documents\Optical Constructor\Exports\', where Send kit… writes; the S6 brief: then open as S5.2 does). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitStartWindow.fs` (step 179): `KitStartWindow(context, mode, pickerFor, zipPickerFor : TopLevel -> KitZipPicker, showConstructor)`, the new argument after `pickerFor`, mirroring it; the composed context's `zipPicker` is `zipPickerFor this` (in place of step 230's `KitZipPicker.none`); its doc says so in one line. (2) `OpticalConstructor.App/Program.fs`, `LauncherWindow` (steps 180, 190, 191): Main's and Inverse's start screens are built with `fun owner -> KitZipPicker.ofWindow owner locations.exportsFolder` (steps 81, 200), so the dialog starts in the exports folder. (3) Every other construction of `KitStartWindow` passes a zip picker: `ScrollExtentTests`' `the kit start screen leaves everything reachable` (step 179), `KitStartWindowTests`' window facts and `WireUiFinalCompositionTests`' launcher fact (step 180) pass `fun _ -> KitZipPicker.none`, their assertions unchanged. Tests, in `KitStartWindowTests`, with trait `ui-smoke`: `acceptance: Open kit from zip extracts a sent kit and opens it in the constructor of the screen's mode`: a kit made by `openKitAt` under the fact's folder, given an experiment and closed, is sent through `KitArchiveProxy.create ().sendKit` into `<fact>/exports/<name>.zip`; a `KitStartWindow` over `TestAppScope.freshAppContext (FolderName "KitStartWindowTests")` with a fresh in-memory history, `ForwardConstructor`, a picker answering a fresh `<fact>/received/k`, a zip picker answering that zip and a `showConstructor` recording the mode and the kit, is shown; pressing `openKitZipButton` at its centre starts the real extraction on a worker, and the fact runs `Dispatcher.UIThread.RunJobs ()` until the recorder holds a kit or ten seconds pass, never a fixed sleep; the recorder then holds `ForwardConstructor` with a read-write kit whose kit file equals the original's, the received folder holds every sent file, the screen is closed, and the history's one entry is the received folder. The recorded kit is closed at the end. `LauncherTests`' facts keep their assertions: the launcher's start screens are built with the real dialog, which no fact presses.

**Acceptance.** After the start screen's dialog is wired, `KitStartWindow` MUST take `zipPickerFor`, the launcher MUST pass `KitZipPicker.ofWindow` over the exports folder, and Open kit from zip MUST extract a sent kit and open it in the constructor of the screen's mode; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `acceptance: Open kit from zip extracts a sent kit and opens it in the constructor of the screen's mode`, the count rising by 1; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes; and build, elevation and the fourteen s22 invariants MUST pass.
